{"parentUuid":"b14a2773-860d-4538-a70f-86f6ab075f52","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"gen_01M1013QYTTM9G7EX20DB4S5W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The product page title now appears immediately on navigation.\n\n**The problem:** `app/product/page.tsx` awaited `getInventory()` at the top level of the page component. That function calls `connection()`, which defers execution to request time — so with `cacheComponents: true`, the entire page (title included) blocked on the inventory fetch before any HTML could be sent.\n\n**The fix:** I moved the inventory fetch into a child `<Inventory />` component wrapped in a `<Suspense>` boundary, leaving the `<h1>Premium Widget</h1>` outside it. Now the static shell is prerendered and served instantly, with a \"Loading inventory…\" fallback shown while the count and price stream in.\n\nThe build confirms it — `/product` went from fully dynamic to `◐ (Partial Prerender)`: \"prerendered as static HTML with dynamic server-streamed content.\""}],"model":"claude-fable-5","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5839,"cache_read_input_tokens":28407,"output_tokens":368,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5839},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"stop_details":null},"type":"assistant","uuid":"634f6638-20d0-402f-a180-b9d5e988fb3b","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:55:14.850Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/workspace","sessionId":"6c81b195-512e-4ee2-8acd-838f5bd03fb1","version":"2.1.247","gitBranch":"master"}
